          model: "Cycle Hub, because its current ratio of 2.00:1 shows $2 of current assets for every $1 of short-term debt, compared with only $1.30 for Wheels Ltd, whose current liabilities of $150,000 are large relative to its liquid resources. The bank would also want to see the liquid ratios and the cash flows before deciding.",
          points: ["Cycle Hub identified as the safer borrower (1)", "Reason: current ratio 2.00:1 against 1.30:1 gives more cover for short-term debts (1)"],
